						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Wednesday, October 16, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">EQ Atlas and Planes of Power Info </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hello all, <BR><BR>I just recieved my Everquest Atlas.  Thought I would share some of the Planes of Power info from it.<BR><BR>From the Plane of Knowledge you'll be able to port to:<BR>1. Cabilis<BR>2. Grobb<BR>3. Neriak<BR>4. Oggok<BR>5. Overthere<BR>6. Paineel<BR>7. Nexus<BR>8. Great Divide<BR>9. Shar Vahl<BR>10. Qeynos<BR>11. Plane of Tranquility<BR>12. Firiona Vie<BR>13. Freeport<BR>14. Ak'anon<BR>15. Rivervale<BR>16. Kelethin<BR>17. Kaladim<BR>18. Halas<BR>19. Felwithe<BR>20. Erudin<BR><BR>It appears the Plane of Knowledge will have Guild Trainers for every class, Spells for each class, and plenty of Tradeskills supplies. Along with a heathy dose of quests.<BR><BR><BR>Here's a over view of all the PoP zones covered in the atlas.<BR>The Bastion of Thunder - Located in the Plane of Storms. Home of Karana, The Rainkeeper.<BR>The Crypt of Decay - Located in the Plane of Disease. Home of Bertoxxulous, The Plaguebringer<BR>The Fortress of Zek Drunder - Located in the Plane of War. Home of Rallos Zek, The Warlord<BR>The Halls of Honor - Location Plane of Valor. Home of Mithaniel Marr, The Truthbringer.<BR>The Plane of Air - Location Unknown. Home of Xegony, Goddess of Air<BR>The Plane of Disease - Can be entered from the Plane of Tranquility.  Entrance to the Crypt of Decay.<BR>The Plane of Earth - Home to The Rathe, a council of 13 individuals with a single consciousness.<BR>The Plane of Fire - Home of Fennin Ro, The Tyrant of Fire.<BR>The Plane of Innovation - This is an industrial wasteland that surrounds a massive factory. Can be reached from the Plane of Tranquility<BR>The Plane of Justice - Home of The Tribunal. Can be reached from the Plane of Tranquility<BR>The Plane of Knowledge - This Realm contains the city of Tanaan. Contains portals to many places in norath and luclin. The Plane of Tranquility can be reached from here.<BR>The Plane of Nightmares - Can be reached from The Plane of Tranquility. Home of Terris-Thule, The Dream Scorcher, the daughter of Cazic.<BR>The Plane of Storms - Controlled by Karana and is home to Storm Giants.<BR>The Plane of Torment - Location Unknown. Home of Saryn, Mistress of Torment<BR>The Plane of Tranquility - Can be reached from the Plane of Knowledge. Home of Quellious, The Goddess of Tranquility. You can travel to the Planes of Disease, Nightmare, Justice, Innovation and Knowledge from here.<BR>The Plane of Valor - This is a challenge area for those who wish to enter the Halls of Honor.<BR>The Plane of War - Realm of endless war. Home of Tallon and Vallon, Sons of Zek.<BR>The Plane of Water - a 2 level Coral Reef. Home to Coirnav, The Avatar of Water.<BR>and finally ...<BR>The Tower of Solusek Ro - Located in the Plane of Fire. This tower contains 5 different dungeons. Home of Solusek Ro, The Burning Prince.<BR><BR><BR>There's quite a lot history about the Planes of Power in the Atlas and if you want more information go buy the book! <BR><BR>Aside from the interesting sneak peek at Planes of Power the rest of the Atlas is almost a dead on copy of <a href=http://www.eqatlas.com>EQ Atlas</A>. The maps have been changed a bit and have a slight 3D appearance to them. <BR><BR>Over all I think the EQ Atlas is worth picking up if you can spare the $19.99. Just don't expect a printed version of your favorite spoiler site. There are no LOCS given on the maps. But there is a map for EVERY zone in the game today, including Ssra Temple, Temple of Veeshan, Sleeper's Tomb, Veeshan's Peak and all current Planes.  Vex Thal does have a spot in the Book but no map.
							<br><BR>
							 - Ganza<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=323">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Wednesday, October 02, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Updating Guilds </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hmm, was edditing my thread & it deleted :(  So here it is again.<BR><BR>Ok, I am on an update spree again.  Please take a look at the Guild listings and make sure your guild is listed and has the appropriate link that is working.  I will be disabling all non working links and then update as we get the correct ones.  Thanks gang :)<BR>  Alea Jacta Est<BR> Arcane Asylum<BR> Avalanche of Power<BR> Avengers Federation<BR> Avengers of Wrath<BR> BASHIN ORDUR!!<BR> Battle Forged<BR> Black Dawn Elite<BR> Blackwing<BR> Blades of Light<BR> Blood of Ro<BR> Blood Tide<BR> Bloodstone Templars<BR> Bund des Geistes<BR> Bunnies of Chaos<BR> Champions of the Firebeetle Eye<BR> Circle of the Forgotten<BR> Clan Donald<BR> Corona Mundi<BR> Council of Hate<BR> Cult of the Ancient Wurm<BR> Custos Pondera<BR> Dark Hour<BR> Darkblood<BR> Dealers of Death<BR> Decent Folks<BR> Destiny<BR> Diablos de Hispania<BR> Disciples<BR> Divine Sanction<BR> Dog Soldiers<BR> Drachentaenzer<BR> Draconian Mist<BR> Draken<BR> Elder Dragons<BR> Elven Society<BR> Enchanted Circle<BR> Eye of Mordor<BR> Fate's Union<BR> Fellowship of Lotz<BR> Fire<BR> Flamma Aeturnus<BR> Followers of Set<BR> Forgotten Elite<BR> Furious Pantaloons<BR> Gathered Might<BR> Guardians of K'Arnon<BR> Guardians of the Crystal Rose<BR> Guild of Avalon<BR> Hands of Truth<BR> Hermandad<BR> Illumin Cathari<BR> Immortal Legion of Revenge<BR> Incursores Infernales<BR> Infinite Legacy<BR> Jaggedpine Defenders<BR> Keeper of Balance<BR> Knights of Evermore<BR> Knights of Sacrifice<BR> Knights of the Silver Eagle<BR> Lanakila<BR> Leet For Life<BR> Legion of Dawn<BR> Legion of the White Rose<BR> Les Chevaliers du Lys<BR> Lords of Prophecy<BR> Lords of the Zodiac<BR> Lux Aeterna <BR> Magna Charta<BR> Magnus<BR> Magnus Opus<BR> Majestic Partisans<BR> Mantra<BR> Midnight<BR> Might Of Norrath<BR> Milites Conductiti Caliginis<BR> Moonwhisper<BR> Mystic Gods<BR> Mystical Heroes<BR> Najenas Erben<BR> Noble Dreams<BR> Nomad<BR> Nova Militia Templ